== 1. r1 solves at depth 2, though its template is depth 3 ==
intended r1 : set_cell(set_cell(#0, sub(#1, 1), #2, read(#0, #1, #2)), #1, #2, 0)   (2 free INT params)

move_cell_up-00      -> set_cell(set_cell(input, 1, 0, 0), 0, 0, read(input, 1, 0))
move_cell_up-01      -> set_cell(set_cell(input, 2, 1, 0), 1, 1, read(input, 0, 2))

Note task -01: it reads (0,2) to write (1,1) -- a coincidence fit that holds only because
those cells share a colour in both train examples. A task collision, not a solution.

